.TH ZEX-REMOVE 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-remove \- remove installed packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex remove
.RI [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ \-\-force ]
.IR <package> ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex remove
uninstalls one or more packages from Zainium OS.
.PP
The list of files to remove is read verbatim from the receipt at
.IR /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/<name>.toml .
No glob scanning or filesystem heuristics are used: exactly the files
recorded at install time are removed.
.PP
Before removal,
.B zex remove
checks whether any other installed package depends on the target. If a
reverse dependency exists and
.B \-\-force
is not set, the operation is aborted.
.PP
Pinned packages cannot be removed without first running
.BR "zex unpin <pkg>" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show which files would be removed without making any changes.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Remove even if reverse dependencies exist or files are missing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Package removed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Package not installed, pinned, reverse-dependency conflict, or permission error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex remove ripgrep
    elevate zex remove vim htop --dry-run
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /overlayer/zexlib/registry/installed/<name>.toml
Receipt read to determine which files to remove. Deleted on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-install (1),
.BR zex-inspect (1),
.BR zex-history (1)
